      "text": "To find the value of the 25th term of the arithmetic sequence \\(2, 5, 8, \\ldots\\), we start by identifying the first term and the common difference of the sequence.\n\nThe first term \\(a\\) of the sequence is:\n\\[a = 2\\]\n\nThe common difference \\(d\\) is the difference between any two consecutive terms. For example, the difference between the second term and the first term is:\n\\[d = 5 - 2 = 3\\]\n\nThe general formula for the \\(n\\)-th term of an arithmetic sequence is given by:\n\\[a_n = a + (n-1)d\\]\n\nWe need to find the 25th term, so we substitute \\(n = 25\\), \\(a = 2\\), and \\(d = 3\\) into the formula:\n\\[a_{25} = 2 + (25-1) \\cdot 3\\]\n\nFirst, calculate \\(25-1\\):\n\\[25-1 = 24\\]\n\nNext, multiply 24 by 3:\n\\[24 \\cdot 3 = 72\\]\n\nFinally, add this result to the first term:\n\\[2 + 72 = 74\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of the 25th term is:\n\\[\\boxed{74}\\]",
