      "text": "To find the value of the 25th term of the arithmetic sequence \\(2, 5, 8, \\ldots\\), we need to use the formula for the \\(n\\)-th term of an arithmetic sequence. The general formula for the \\(n\\)-th term \\(a_n\\) of an arithmetic sequence is given by:\n\n\\[\na_n = a_1 + (n-1)d\n\\]\n\nwhere:\n- \\(a_n\\) is the \\(n\\)-th term,\n- \\(a_1\\) is the first term,\n- \\(d\\) is the common difference,\n- \\(n\\) is the term number.\n\nFor the given sequence \\(2, 5, 8, \\ldots\\):\n- The first term \\(a_1\\) is 2.\n- The common difference \\(d\\) is the difference between consecutive terms, which is \\(5 - 2 = 3\\).\n\nWe need to find the 25th term, so \\(n = 25\\). Substituting these values into the formula, we get:\n\n\\[\na_{25} = 2 + (25-1) \\cdot 3\n\\]\n\nFirst, calculate \\(25 - 1\\):\n\n\\[\n25 - 1 = 24\n\\]\n\nNext, multiply 24 by the common difference 3:\n\n\\[\n24 \\cdot 3 = 72\n\\]\n\nFinally, add this result to the first term 2:\n\n\\[\na_{25} = 2 + 72 = 74\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of the 25th term is \\(\\boxed{74}\\).",
